<urn:usf:command-retirement:review:1> <urn:usf:predicate:retirementReason> "The declared shape usf review --candidate DIGEST cannot be implemented as specified. It excludes the route that produced a candidate, and a candidate deliberately carries no producer identity: actual identity lives in execution evidence, which is ignored disposable state and may never become selection authority. Implementing the declared shape needs a candidate-envelope change rather than a wrapper. The capability it names is delivered: review-diverse is an implemented routing strategy selecting across distinct provider families and distinct underlying model families, reachable through usf route." <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
