<urn:usf:profile-disposition-set:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dispositionBasis> "Derived on 2026-09-03 from the contract-selection lattice over all nine declared RealisationProfiles. Contract-set containment is the objective relation: where profile A's selectsContract set is a strict subset of profile B's, B carries every obligation A selects. The chain is v3-semantic-first:1 (1 contract) subset of v3-self-host:1 (5) subset of v3-self-host:2 (6) subset of v3-self-host-hermes:1 (7) subset of the product BAU lane (8), with the product bootstrap lane (1) subset of the product ordinary lane (7) subset of hermes-bau:1. v3-self-host:3 (12 contracts, nine of them selected by nothing else) is not in that chain: it is a re-selection onto the provider pipeline and the only policy-covered lane. v3-semantic-recovery:1 owns semantic-recovery-exchange:1 uniquely and is subsumed by nothing." <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
<urn:usf:profile-disposition-set:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "an-uncovered-lane-is-not-a-defect-policy-admission-is-a-precondition-the-corpus-states-deliberately" <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
<urn:usf:profile-disposition-set:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "subsumed-means-contract-set-containment-not-that-the-successor-completed-the-predecessors-work" <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
<urn:usf:profile-disposition-set:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "these-are-recorded-product-decisions-not-derivations-the-lattice-is-evidence-for-them-not-a-proof-of-them" <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
