<urn:usf:supersession:self-host-profile-lineage:1> <urn:usf:predicate:reason> "Profile identity is part of completion identity, so a work completed under one profile reads ineligible under another even when its bytes are unchanged. Three self-host profile revisions accumulated as the selection boundary moved: revision 1 for the bootstrap lane, revision 2 when provider qualification was selected, revision 3 for the current provider pipeline. Only revision 3 carries publication policies for the works its manifest selects, so only revision 3 can reach completion. Without this record an operator reads thirty-four manifest-by-profile lanes, thirty-three of which report outstanding work, and cannot tell which one is live." <urn:usf:graph:foundation> .
